    seoTitle: 'International Online School & Homeschool Uganda | Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level & IB — Smartious',
    seoDesc: 'Premium international online school for Ugandan families. Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, IB Diploma and Pearson Edexcel taught live in East Africa Time. For families in Kampala, Entebbe, Wakiso and across Uganda. From USD 180/month (≈ UGX 675,000).',
    localFacts: ['Kampala · Entebbe · Wakiso · Mukono', 'Cambridge & British Council exam centres', 'Live EAT classes + recordings'],
    pains: 'Uganda has a small but expensive international school market. Premium Kampala schools — International School of Uganda (ISU), Kampala International School (KISU), Lincoln International School — charge UGX 50,000,000-85,000,000 per year for primary and even more at IBDP level. Mid-tier international schools (Acorns, British School of Kampala, Kabojja, Galaxy) sit at UGX 22,000,000-40,000,000. Add ISSA league fees, transport, uniforms and exam fees (UGX 4-12M per session) and a single child at a top Kampala school easily costs over UGX 100 million a year. At the same time, Uganda\'s regulatory framework for home and online education is in transition — the National Curriculum Development Centre is actively drafting a homeschool policy, and the Attorney General has clarified that pure homeschooling without local school registration is not yet provided for under existing law. Smartious is built for Kampala-resident families who want a Cambridge, A-Level or IB pathway with global university recognition, the academic depth of a real international school, and fees that come in at a meaningful fraction of the premium tier — typically used alongside enrolment at a local Ugandan school for regulatory clarity, or as the substantive academic programme for expat families.',
    curricula: ['Cambridge IGCSE', 'Cambridge A-Level', 'IB MYP', 'IB Diploma', 'Pearson Edexcel International', 'British National Curriculum (Primary)', 'American Curriculum Support'],
    regulation: 'Uganda\'s regulatory framework for home and online education is currently in transition. The Education Act and 1995 Constitution recognise parental responsibility for their children\'s education (Articles 31(4) and 34(2)). In November 2024, however, the Attorney General clarified that homeschooling — defined as withdrawing children from formal school registration entirely — is not yet provided for under existing law. Meanwhile, the National Curriculum Development Centre has been actively conducting a baseline study (approximately 7,000 children currently homeschooled in Uganda) and is drafting a homeschool policy in collaboration with Home-Scholars Uganda Group (HUG). The Ministry of Education permanent secretary has acknowledged that homeschooling policy is in development. Practical implications for Smartious families: (1) Expat families resident in Uganda can use Smartious freely — international online education for expatriate children operates in a separate context from Ugandan citizen regulation. (2) Ugandan citizen families typically use Smartious as the substantive academic programme alongside enrolment at a local Ugandan or international school (which handles formal registration and UNEB or international exam pathway). (3) For pure homeschoolers without any local school registration, families should consult with the Home-Scholars Uganda Group and monitor the upcoming NCDC policy. We are honest about this complexity during admissions.',
    examCentres: 'Cambridge IGCSE, Cambridge A-Level and Pearson Edexcel examinations are sat at British Council Uganda exam centres in Kampala and at authorised international school centres. International School of Uganda (ISU) and British School of Kampala both host examination centres accepting private candidates. IB Diploma examinations are administered through authorised IB World Schools in Uganda. Smartious handles all examination registration, advises families on the most convenient centre, and runs comprehensive mock examination programmes before the May/June and October/November series. Cambridge and Edexcel exam fees are separate from Smartious tuition (typically UGX 4-12 million per session depending on subject combination).',
    testimonial: '',
